[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3761947355","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114764#issuecomment-3761947355","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114764","id":3761947355,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gOsLb","user":{"login":"wlsnmrk","id":23439518,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNDM5NTE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23439518?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlsnmrk","html_url":"https://github.com/wlsnmrk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlsnmrk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlsnmrk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlsnmrk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlsnmrk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlsnmrk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlsnmrk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlsnmrk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlsnmrk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wlsnmrk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-16T21:51:28Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T21:51:28Z","body":"Thanks for putting this fix together! \r\n\r\nA suggestion: it might be preferable, instead of returning early, to let the playback construction proceed and then call `set_stream_paused(!node->can_process())` at the end of `play_basic()`, before the return.\r\n\r\nAdvantages:\r\n* It leaves the playback queued for when the tree resumes, instead of discarding the call to `play_basic()`\r\n* It's analogous to the behavior in `notification()` at line 97\r\n* I believe it would fix the TODO in `set_stream_paused()` at line 178 (181 in your modified version), which seems likely to be the root of #114694","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3761947355/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3762389340","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114764#issuecomment-3762389340","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114764","id":3762389340,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gQYFc","user":{"login":"neclor","id":81529592,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNTI5NTky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81529592?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor","html_url":"https://github.com/neclor","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-17T00:43:14Z","updated_at":"2026-01-17T12:02:06Z","body":"You're right, your suggestion makes more sense.\r\n\r\nI noticed that `VideoStreamPlayer` handles this by manually triggering the pause notification:\r\n```cpp\r\nvoid VideoStreamPlayer::play() {\r\n\t//...\r\n\tif (!can_process()) {\r\n\t\t_notification(NOTIFICATION_PAUSED);\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n```\r\nI think we should follow the same pattern in `AudioStreamPlayerInternal`\r\nSomething like:\r\n```cpp\r\nif (!node->can_process()) {\r\n\tnotification(Node::NOTIFICATION_PAUSED);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3762389340/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3762406270","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114764#issuecomment-3762406270","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114764","id":3762406270,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gQcN-","user":{"login":"neclor","id":81529592,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNTI5NTky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81529592?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor","html_url":"https://github.com/neclor","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-17T00:50:59Z","updated_at":"2026-01-17T00:50:59Z","body":"I don't think this will resolve the TODO in `set_stream_paused()`. To fix it, we would need a new variable to save the pause state even when there is no stream.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3762406270/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4638584252","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114764#issuecomment-4638584252","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114764","id":4638584252,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFHstvA","user":{"login":"Joy-less","id":65855333,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1ODU1MzMz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65855333?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less","html_url":"https://github.com/Joy-less","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Joy-less/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-06T12:33:39Z","updated_at":"2026-06-06T12:33:39Z","body":"Does this also need to apply to `AudioStreamPlayer3D` and `AudioStreamPlayer2D`?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4638584252/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4642205534","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114764#issuecomment-4642205534","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114764","id":4642205534,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFLJvXg","user":{"login":"neclor","id":81529592,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNTI5NTky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81529592?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor","html_url":"https://github.com/neclor","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-07T10:23:31Z","updated_at":"2026-06-07T10:28:01Z","body":"No, they are already working as expected. In `AudioStreamPlayer2D` and `3D`, sound depends on a physical process that is not running during pause.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4642205534/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5599140611","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114764#issuecomment-5599140611","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114764","id":5599140611,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTbwbAw","user":{"login":"neclor","id":81529592,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxNTI5NTky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81529592?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor","html_url":"https://github.com/neclor","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neclor/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-09T08:52:31Z","updated_at":"2026-09-09T08:52:31Z","body":"> Potential workaround could be to not start the playback, but save the state for the playback to start on `NOTIFICATION_UNPAUSED` from `AudioStreamPlayer`.\r\n\r\nI tried this approach: \r\ndon't start the playback at all while `!can_process()`. \r\n`play()` queues the position in `deferred_plays`;\r\n`_flush_deferred_plays()` starts them on `NOTIFICATION_UNPAUSED / UNSUSPENDED / ENTER_TREE`, \r\n`stop()` clears the queue. \r\nSo nothing reaches the audio thread until the node can process.\r\n\r\nTested manually: \r\n`play()` with and without pause, \r\nadding/removing the node while paused and while running, \r\nre-entering the tree, \r\nrepeated `play()` during pause - all behave as expected","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5599140611/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]